ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "SGLang HiCache", url: "https://docs.sglang.ai/advanced_features/hicache_design.html", overlap: "Hierarchical KV cache with GPU L1, host-memory L2, distributed L3; local match, prefetch, write-back policies; docs explicitly target multi-QA/long-context and multi-turn dialogue with async decode KV offload. Strong overlap with tiered KV offload/prefetch, but I did not find evidence that it schedules the full host round trip specifically against an agent inter-turn idle gap distribution."},
  {system: "vLLM v1 KV offload", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/tree/main/vllm/v1/kv_offload", overlap: "Shipping scheduler-side OffloadingManager with lookup, prepare_load, prepare_store, complete_load/store, CPU and tiering backends. Strong overlap on KV offload/load/store machinery; no found agent-gap-timed policy."},
  {system: "LMCache async_loading", url: "https://docs.lmcache.ai/kv_cache/async_loading.html", overlap: "Decouples scheduler lookup from worker-side prefetch/retrieval, performs tiered async contains and non-blocking gets over LocalCPU/LocalDisk/remote backends to overlap I/O and compute. Strong overlap on async KV retrieval/prefetch; no found inter-turn-gap scheduler."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM KV cache reuse + host offload", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html#offloading-to-host-memory", overlap: "Reuses KV pages for same-prefix requests and copies reusable blocks to pinned host memory instead of evicting, onboarding when reused. Strong overlap on host KV offload/onboard; not agent-idle-gap timed."},
  {system: "SGLang RadixAttention", url: "https://www.lmsys.org/blog/2024-01-17-sglang/", overlap: "Caches reusable prefix KV across structured/multi-call LLM programs; adjacent to agent multi-turn prefix reuse, but primarily GPU-resident prefix caching, not CPU demote+prefetch against idle gaps."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: design
SCALE_REALISM: Holds only as a modeled win-region, not yet at realistic workload. The packet’s own L0 says prefetch wins in 93.5% of swept cells but loses in 6.5%, with 70% of losses PCIe-BW-bound; the sane-deployment box has 1 loss out of 7560 cells. That is useful scoping, but realistic scale is still insufficient evidence because PCIe/NVLink-C2C contention, active decode traffic, real vLLM/LMCache/SGLang resume TTFT, real agent inter-turn gap distribution, and real re-reference probability are unmeasured.
RATIONALE: Yellow because no cited shipping system found in this sweep explicitly implements “agent-inter-turn-gap-timed proactive demote + prefetch” as the policy, but most underlying mechanism is already shipping in SGLang HiCache, vLLM KV offload, LMCache async loading, and TensorRT-LLM host KV offload. The contribution is therefore not KV offload/prefetch itself; it is the scheduling design hypothesis that known agent idle gaps can hide the round trip. The packet’s artifact is reproducible at L0 from committed pre-registration plus CSV-backed CPU-only simulation, and it honestly rejects universal “strictly better Pareto.” It cannot be green until tested in a real serving stack against the above systems, with measured concurrent D2H/H2D bandwidth and real agent traces.
